27 \u2014 the noun from request."},{"answer":"confusing","accept":[],"options":["confusing","confused","confusion","confusingly"],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"She gave a very ___ (CONFUSE) explanation of the rules.","hint":"adjective: causing confusion","explanation":"\u0027Confusing\u0027 describes something that causes confusion; \u0027confused\u0027 describes the person affected."},{"answer":"calm","accept":[],"options":["calm","calmness","calmly","calming"],"base":null,"keyword":null,"lead":null,"sentence":"The police appealed for ___ (CALM).","hint":"noun after \u0027for\u0027","explanation":"\u0027Appealed for calm\u0027 \u2014 the set phrase uses \u0027calm\u0027 as noun."}]}